cessible name.\\n*Suggested fix:* Add an accessible name, for example: <input type=\\\"image\\\" src=\\\"pay-now.png\\\" alt=\\\"Pay now\\\" width=\\\"120\\\" height=\\\"40\\\"> or add aria-label=\\\"Pay now\\\" if alt cannot be used.\"},{\"summary\":\"Select element #promo lacks an accessible name\",\"priority\":\"Highest\",\"labels\":[\"a11y\",\"wcag-4.1.2\",\"select-name\"],\"description\":\"*WCAG 4.1.2* Name, Role, Value\\n*Element:* #promo\\n*Affected users:* blind users, screen reader users, voice control users, motor-impaired keyboard-only users\\n*Steps:*\\n1. Open fixtures/holdout/checkout-payment.html\\n2. Navigate to the payment section\\n3. Locate the promo code dropdown\\n*Expected:* The select control must have a programmatically determinable name so that assistive technologies can announce its purpose (e.g., \\\"Promo code\\\").\\n*Actual:* The <select id=\\\"promo\\\"> element has no associated <label>, no aria-label, no aria-labelledby, and no title attribute, resulting in no accessible name.\\n*Suggested fix:* Add a visible label and associate it with the select, e.g., <label for=\\\"promo\\\">Promo code</label> before the <select>, or add aria-label=\\\"Promo code\\\" to the select element.\"},{\"summary\":\"Missing persistent labels for payment form fields\",\"priority\":\"Highest\",\"labels\":[\"a11y\",\"wcag-3.3.2\",\"placeholder-only-label\"],\"description\":\"*WCAG 3.3.2* Labels or Instructions\\n*Element:* #pay-name\\n*Affected users:* blind users, screen reader users, low vision users, cognitive disability users\\n*Steps:*\\n1. Open fixtures/holdout/checkout-payment.html\\n2. Navigate to the payment section\\n3. Focus on the input with id=\\\"pay-name\\\"\\n4. Observe that only placeholder text \\\"Name on card\\\" is announced\\n5. Repeat for the input with id=\\\"pay-card\\\"\\n*Expected:* Each form input must have a persistent visible label (or an accessible name via aria-label, aria-labelledby, or title) that is announced by screen readers and remains visible when the user types.\\n*Actual:* The inputs #pay-name and #pay-card rely solely on placeholder text for identification; no <label>, aria-label, aria-labelledby, or title is provided.\\n*Suggested fix:* Add a <label> element associated with each input and remove reliance on placeholder as the sole label. Example:\\n\\n<label for=\\\"pay-name\\\" class=\\\"sr-only\\\">Name on card</label>\\n<input type=\\\"text\\\" id=\\\"pay-name\\\" placeholder=\\\"Name on card\\\" aria-required=\\\"true\\\">\\n\\n<label for=\\\"pay-card\\\" class=\\\"sr-only\\\">Card number</label>\\n<input type=\\\"text\\\" id=\\\"pay-card\\\" placeholder=\\\"Card number\\\" aria-required=\\\"true\\\">\"}],\"alert\":true,\"alertMessage\":\"A11Y ALERT: 4 critical accessibility bug(s) on file://C:\\\\Users\\\\sharvari.warudkar\\\\a11y-auto-triage\\\\fixtures\\\\holdout\\\\checkout-payment.html\"}"
