                          "description": "*WCAG 4.1.2* Name, Role, Value\n*Element:* a.icon-link[href=\"/cart\"]\n*Affected users:* blind users, keyboard-only users\n*Steps:*\n1. Open fixtures/holdout/home.html in a browser\n2. Tab through the page until the cart link is focused\n3. Listen with a screen reader or observe that no link text is announced\n*Expected:* The link should have a discernible accessible name that is announced by screen readers and visible to assistive technologies.\n*Actual:* The <a href=\"/cart\" class=\"icon-link\"></a> element is focusable but has no visible text, aria-label, aria-labelledby, or title attribute, resulting in no accessible name.\n*Suggested fix:* Add an accessible name, e.g., <a href=\"/cart\" class=\"icon-link\" aria-label=\"View cart\"></a>, or include visible text inside the link."
